{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The burnt-offering of the sabbath on its sabbath.</b> And not the burnt-offering of one sabbath on another sabbath — were its day to pass, I would hear that he offers two on the following sabbath. Therefore Scripture says ״בְּשַׁבָּתוֹ״ — this teaches that if its day passed, its offering is void (Sifrei)." "<b>Beside the burnt-offering of the tamid.</b> These are the musaf offerings, apart from those two lambs of the tamid burnt-offering. And it teaches that they are offered only between the two tamid offerings; and so in all the musaf offerings it says ״beside the burnt-offering of the tamid״ for this teaching."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:09.029927269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}